UPDATE companies SET description='Quantum Composers is based in Bozeman, Montana, where it has designed and manufactured precision timing and photonics instruments for more than three decades.

The product line centers on digital delay generators, pulse generators, current generators, and laser systems, including Nd:YAG lasers. Quantum Composers also provides custom engineering services such as FPGA and firmware development, multi-board synchronization architectures, and environmental hardening for vibration, temperature, or radiation. The firm supports OEM customers through full lifecycle and production support, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Customers include university research labs, aerospace and defense contractors, medical and dental device manufacturers, and spectroscopy and material science facilities. A noted example is a regenerative periodontal therapy device maker that engaged Quantum Composers to double production of 6-watt free-running variable dental lasers. The company also supplies current pulsers and firesets for pyrotechnics and aerospace applications.

Quantum Composers emphasizes collaborative design, stating it does not simply sell timing devices but works to build precision into the design from day one. It backs its instruments with multi-year warranties and lifetime service, and offers re-calibration, programming assistance, and RMA support through its photonics experts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Digital delay generator design and manufacturing", "Pulse generator design and manufacturing", "Current generator design and manufacturing", "Laser system design and manufacturing (including Nd:YAG)", "Custom electro-optics instrument development", "FPGA and firmware customization", "Multi-board synchronization architecture design", "Environmental hardening (vibration, temperature, radiation)", "Lifecycle and production support for OEM customers", "Service, programming assistance, re-calibration, and RMA", "Driver and firmware downloads", "Global reseller and distributor network"], "industries": ["Research and Universities", "Aerospace and defense", "Medical, dental, and life sciences", "Spectroscopy", "Material science"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Nd:YAG Lasers", "Pulse Generators", "Current Generators", "Digital Delay Generators", "Synchronization Systems", "Custom Timing Solutions"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Up to 5ps timing resolution", "built_on": ["Up to 5ps timing resolution on digital delay generators", "Multi-channel synchronization and ultra-low jitter performance", "FPGA and firmware customization for OEM timing solutions", "Multi-year warranties and lifetime service on all instruments", "Lifecycle and production support for OEM customers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bozeman, Montana -> db", "Over 30 years in business -> page /", "Manufactures digital delay generators, pulse generators, current generators, laser systems -> page /", "Provides custom engineering: FPGA & firmware customization, multi-board synchronization, environmental hardening -> page /", "Serves research, aerospace and defense, medical/dental/life sciences, spectroscopy, material science -> page /", "Offers multi-year warranties and lifetime service -> page /", "Has global resellers and distributors -> page /", "Produced 200 6-watt free-running variable dental lasers for periodontal therapy device manufacturer -> db", "Offers service, programming assistance, re-calibration, RMA -> db", "Products include Particle Image Velocimetry -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For 30 years, we have been offering pulse generators, and custom electro-optics instruments.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quantum-composers' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Quarter Sawn Millwork Group operates from New York City, serving the five boroughs as well as New Jersey and Connecticut. The company describes its team as master craftsmen with more than 30 years of experience, though a specific founding year is not published. Ownership structure and founder names are not disclosed in the available material.

The shop combines millwork, glasswork, and metalwork under one roof, handling design, fabrication, and installation without subcontracting. A full weld shop, a dedicated glass shop, and advanced CNC equipment—including Thermwood 3‑axis and 5‑axis machines—allow production of custom built‑ins, radiator covers, Murphy beds, bathroom vanities, kitchens, walk‑in closets, and one‑off furniture pieces. Projects range from single residential items to multi‑floor commercial build‑outs such as hotel lobbies, airline lounges, and full restaurant renovations.

Clients span hospitality, retail, commercial office, and high‑end residential sectors. Named accounts include Irving Farm Coffee Roasters, Partners Coffee, Le Pain Quotidien, The Gap, Saks Fifth Avenue, Estée Lauder, Air France, Turkish Airlines, Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP, The Mercer Hotel, The Shubert Theater Group, and numerous other NYC venues. The firm has also collaborated with general contractors such as LCM Construction on projects like the Bedford, Brooklyn Partners Coffee location.

QSMG emphasizes that its in‑house model—designers, fabricators, and installers working together—delivers consistent quality and accountability. The company highlights its agility and turnaround speed despite a small team, and points to its ELLE Decor feature for the Gramercy Park Penthouse project as external validation of its craftsmanship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom millwork", "Glass fabrication", "Metal welding and fabrication", "CNC machining (3-axis, 5-axis)", "Custom furniture making", "Custom cabinetry", "Built-in furniture", "Radiator cover fabrication", "Murphy bed fabrication", "Bathroom vanity fabrication", "Custom kitchen fabrication", "Walk-in closet systems", "Installation services", "Upholstery", "Reclaimed wood milling", "High-gloss finishing", "Gold leaf application", "LED lighting integration", "Structural steel engineering", "Project design and engineering"], "industries": ["Hospitality (hotels, restaurants, coffee shops)", "Retail", "Commercial office", "Residential", "Aviation (airline lounges)", "Legal services", "Healthcare and wellness"], "materials": ["White oak", "Rift-cut white oak", "Reclaimed wood", "Glass", "Steel", "Gold leaf", "High-gloss finishes"], "equipment": ["Thermwood CNC machines (3-axis, 5-axis)", "Full weld shop equipment", "Glass shop equipment"], "volume": "Custom one-offs to large-scale commercial build-outs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Entirely in\u2011house design, fabrication, and installation with no subcontracting", "Full weld shop, glass shop, and Thermwood CNC (3\u2011axis and 5\u2011axis) on site", "Services all five NYC boroughs plus New Jersey and Connecticut", "Featured in ELLE Decor for the Gramercy Park Penthouse project", "Small, agile team focused on fast turnaround without sacrificing detail"], "facts_used": ["Location: New York, NY -> db", "30+ years experience -> /", "In-house design, fabrication, installation, no subcontracting -> /", "Full weld shop, glass shop, advanced CNC technology -> /", "Thermwood CNC machines (3-axis, 5-axis) -> /", "Services 5 boroughs, NJ, CT -> /", "Clients: Irving Farm Coffee Roasters, Partners Coffee, Le Pain Quotidien, The Gap, Saks Fifth Avenue, Est\u00e9e Lauder, Air France, Turkish Airlines, Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP, The Mercer Hotel, The Shubert Theater Group, etc. -> /", "Projects: hotel build-outs, airline lounges, restaurant renovations, custom furniture, radiator covers, built-ins, Murphy beds, vanities, kitchens, walk-in closets -> /", "ELLE Decor feature for Gramercy Park Penthouse -> /", "Materials: white oak, rift-cut white oak, reclaimed wood, glass, steel, gold leaf -> /", "Collaboration with LCM Construction on Partners Coffee Bedford project -> /", "Instagram: QSM_NYC -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every project is handled entirely in-house. Our designers, fabricators, and installers work together to ensure consistent quality, accountability, and seamless execution\u2014no subcontracting.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.instagram.com/QSM_NYC/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quarter-sawn-millwork-group-custom-woodwork-nyc-qsmg' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Quick Cable Corporation, operating as QuickCable®, is headquartered in Franksville, Wisconsin, with a second manufacturing and distribution site in Mississauga, Ontario. The company was founded in 1946 by Jack Shannon and has grown from a specialty battery maker into a manufacturer of battery connection solutions for commercial and industrial markets.

QuickCable engineers and manufactures a broad portfolio of terminal connectors, cable assemblies, tools, and custom-engineered power solutions. Its in-house capabilities include die-casting, stamping, machining, cable assembly, plastic molding, printing, non-ferrous metal casting, and wire and cable fabrication. The combined facilities support a workforce of approximately 150 employees and serve global distribution.

The company serves industries including material handling, standby power and generation, heavy-duty truck and bus, automotive, recreation, agriculture, electrical, powersports, commercial vehicles, construction, marine, and military/defense. Its customer base comprises OEMs, wire harness assemblers, distributors, dealers, and retailers seeking custom-designed connectors, cable assemblies, and battery accessories.

QuickCable states its mission is to drive customer success through leadership and innovation in the energy storage industry, emphasizing American-made quality and a product offering described as the broadest and most comprehensive in the industry. The company highlights its QuickEverything™ commitment to comprehensive power connectivity solutions and value-added distribution services as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["die-casting", "stamping", "machining", "cable assembly", "plastic molding", "printing", "non-ferrous metal casting", "wire and cable fabrication", "custom design", "value added distribution", "engineering support", "technical support"], "industries": ["Material Handling", "Standby Power & Generation", "Heavy Duty Truck & Bus", "Automotive", "Recreation", "Agriculture", "Electrical", "Powersports", "Commercial Vehicles", "Construction", "Marine", "Military/Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Broadest and most comprehensive product offering in the industry", "In-house die-casting, stamping, machining, cable assembly, plastic molding, and printing", "Custom-engineered connectors and battery cable assemblies for demanding requirements", "Value-added packaging and distribution services", "American-made quality and innovation for over 80 years"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1946 by Jack Shannon -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Franksville, Wisconsin and Mississauga, Ontario -> /about-us", "150 employees -> /about-us", "Manufactures battery connection solutions -> /", "In-house capabilities: die-casting, stamping, machining, cable assembly, plastic molding, printing -> /services", "Industries served: Material Handling, Standby Power & Generation, Heavy Duty Truck & Bus, Automotive, Recreation, Agriculture, Electrical, Powersports -> /", "Custom design and engineering services -> /services", "Value added distribution services -> /services", "Mission: Drive customers'' success through leadership and innovation in energy storage industry -> /about-us", "ISO certification mentioned -> /about-us", "Broadest product offering in industry -> /services", "American-made quality for over 80 years -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "QuickCable is a leading U.S.-based manufacturer of battery connection solutions", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "150", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quick-cable-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The store carries a wide range of quilting cottons, batiks, flannels, and specialty lines such as Liberty, Tilda, and Moda, along with pre-cut bundles, quilt kits, patterns, notions, batting, and interfacing. In addition to retail, the shop offers longarm quilting services and hosts quarterly three-day retreats with catered meals and dedicated sewing stations.

The business serves individual quilters and sewing enthusiasts both in-store and through its online shop, which features live shopping shows every Friday and Monday. Customers include hobbyists seeking curated mystery kits, such as the quarterly Mystery Five-0 series, as well as those purchasing machines and supplies for home studios.

