UPDATE companies SET description='R-K Electronics is based in Mason, Ohio, and traces its roots to February 1949 when Bill Keller and John Runge founded R-K Electric Company, Inc. as a panel builder serving steel mills, machine tool builders, and paper manufacturers across Ohio, Indiana, and Kentucky.

Today the company designs and manufactures a range of electronic automation control components, from intrinsically safe low‑voltage relays to 600‑volt three‑phase monitoring controls. In addition to its standard product line, R-K develops custom processor‑based embedded controllers—dedicated PLCs with hardware, firmware, and packaging tailored to OEM specifications—for equipment and machinery control systems.

R-K’s customers span the electrical controls industry and OEMs in sectors such as heating and refrigeration, pumping and level control, as well as the original steel, machine tool, and paper markets. The company supplies both off‑the‑shelf components and fully customized control solutions built to each OEM’s operating requirements.

The founder’s original decision to start the business because they “couldn’t do any worse working for themselves” evolved into a stated philosophy of customer‑driven innovation: R-K emphasizes listening to customers to create control components with unique features that simplify control requirements and make customers more successful. Ongoing development includes controls that interface with the company’s own color touch screens.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic automation control component design and manufacturing", "Custom processor-based embedded controller design (dedicated PLCs)", "Hardware, firmware, and packaging integration for OEM controls", "Intrinsically safe relay production", "Three-phase monitoring control manufacturing", "Standard product line for heating, refrigeration, pumping, and level control applications"], "industries": ["Steel mills", "Machine tool", "Paper manufacturing", "Electrical controls", "OEM equipment manufacturers", "Heating and refrigeration", "Pumping and level control"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer-driven innovation: develops control components with unique features that simplify control requirements", "Custom processor-based embedded controllers (dedicated PLCs) designed, programmed, and packaged to OEM specifications", "Wide voltage range: from intrinsically safe low-voltage relays to 600V three-phase monitoring controls", "In-house design, firmware, and packaging integration for OEM control systems", "Focus on continuous improvement of manufacturing capabilities and integration with color touch-screen interfaces"], "facts_used": ["Founded February 1949 by Bill Keller and John Runge -> /about", "Started as R-K Electric Company, Inc., panel builder for steel mills, machine tool, paper manufacturing -> /about", "Became largest control panel company in Ohio, Indiana, Kentucky -> /about", "Transitioned to electronics in 1960s-1970s, closed panel business mid-1980s -> /about", "Renamed R-K Electronics in mid-1980s -> /about", "John Keller became sole owner in mid-1980s -> /about", "Headquarters in Mason, Ohio -> db", "Manufactures electronic automation control components: intrinsically safe relays up to 600V three-phase monitoring controls -> /about", "Designs and manufactures custom processor-based embedded controllers (dedicated PLCs) for OEMs -> /about", "Standard product line includes heating & refrigeration, pumping & level control -> /", "Focus on innovation, listening to customers, developing unique features -> /about", "Goal: making customers more successful -> /about", "Developing controls that interface with color touch screens -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, R-K manufactures a wide variety of electronic automation control components for the electrical controls industry.", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='r-k-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='RP Foods was founded in 1999 in Dallas, Texas. The company began working almost exclusively in the Hispanic grocery category, leveraging over 20 years of retail and importing experience among its staff.

The company imports products from Mexico, Asia, and Europe, and operates its own facility in Dallas along with third‑party logistics locations in Laredo, Texas; Atlanta, Georgia; and Montebello, California. It focuses on providing retailers with products that enhance category offerings and meet current shopper demands.

