UPDATE companies SET description='RW Technologies US LLC operates from Crystal Lake, Illinois, a northwest suburb of Chicago. The company was founded in 2011 by Troy Richert and Micheal Walker as a partnership to provide electronic manufacturing services.

The shop specializes in printed circuit board assembly, offering quick-turn prototypes, new product introduction (NPI) runs, and low-to-medium volume production. Its services extend to lead-free and mixed-technology assembly, surface-mount and through-hole placement, repairs and upgrades, parts procurement, component warehousing in an environmentally controlled stockroom, and box-build assembly including custom enclosures and wiring. All work is performed in the company''s own facility outside Chicago.

RW Technologies serves multiple industries, with a noted example of camera modules for the telecommunications sector. Its customer base includes engineers who need fast prototypes, low unit costs, flexible design specifications, and schedule certainty for product launches.

The company differentiates itself through what it calls a Trifold Tech Approach: superior U.S. quality backed by ISO 9001:2015 and IPC-A-610 compliance, quick and flexible turnarounds enabled by lean manufacturing principles, and global cost competitiveness achieved through low overhead and manufacturing efficiencies. The founders emphasize that they are not merely order takers but partners who build each board as if it were their own.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (Prototypes, Quick Turn NPI, Low to Medium Volume)", "Lead-free Assembly", "Mixed Technology Circuit Board Assembly", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-hole Assembly", "Repair, Troubleshooting, and Upgrades", "Parts Procurement / Material Sourcing", "Component Warehousing and Inventory Management", "Box Build Assembly (Systems Integration)", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) Review", "Turnkey Circuit Board Components", "Consignment (Labor-only) Assembly", "Circuit Board Prototyping", "Circuit Board Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to medium volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Superior US Quality (ISO 9001:2015 and IPC-A-610 compliance)", "Quick, Flexible Turnarounds (lean manufacturing principles)", "Global Cost Competitiveness (low overhead, manufacturing efficiencies)", "Environmentally controlled component warehousing", "Not just order takers \u2013 build it right, build it like it''s our own"], "facts_used": ["Company name and description -> db", "Headquarters: Crystal Lake, IL -> db, /", "Founded 2011 by Troy Richert and Micheal Walker -> /about", "Services: PCB assembly, prototypes, low-medium volume, repairs, procurement, warehousing, box build -> /, /about, /services", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, IPC-A-610, RoHS -> /, db", "Industries: telecommunications (camera modules) -> /, /about", "Trifold Tech Approach: Superior US Quality, Quick Flexible Turnarounds, Global Cost Competitiveness -> /, /about", "Facility: all production in-house outside Chicago -> /about", "Team members: Troy Richert (President), Micheal Walker (VP Procurement), Scott Broderick (Quality Manager), Val Bedard (Inventory Control), Bill Perry (Special Projects) -> /about", "Mission: enable customers to rapidly bring new products to market -> /, /about, /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "RW Technologies is a US-based electronic circuit board services company", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='r-w-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='R&D Fabworks, LLC is based in Crittenden, Kentucky, and was founded in 2016 by Garrett Daniels. After studying mechanical engineering at the University of Kentucky and earning AWS certifications at the Knight School of Welding, Daniels spent years in production welding and machining while building the business on nights and weekends. He committed to the company full-time in 2019 with the support of his wife, Amanda, and the shop has since grown from a custom off-road fabrication startup into a full-service metal fabrication and welding operation serving the Cincinnati and Northern Kentucky region.

The company provides custom metal fabrication, welding (MIG, TIG, stick), CNC plasma cutting, plate and sheet rolling, tube rolling and bending, and structural fabrication including mezzanines, catwalks, safety railings, ADA ramps and handrails. It also offers marine construction and repair such as marina builds, boat lifts, and aluminum boat repair, as well as mobile welding for on-site equipment and trailer repair. The shop handles one-off prototypes through large production runs and works with materials ranging from carbon steel and stainless steel to titanium, Inconel, Monel, Hastelloy, copper-nickel alloys, and copper and brass brazing.

R&D Fabworks serves residential homeowners, commercial property owners, contractors, industrial facilities, marinas, and fleet operators primarily within a three-hour radius of Cincinnati. Typical projects include custom staircases, railings, and outdoor structures for homes; safety railings, ADA-compliant access systems, and structural platforms for commercial and industrial buildings; and emergency mobile welding for heavy equipment, trailers, and cast-iron components.

