UPDATE companies SET description='RAUMEDIC is a German medical technology company with a U.S. presence in Mills River, North Carolina. No founding year or founders are disclosed in the provided materials.

The company develops and manufactures polymer-based components and systems for intensive care and biopharma fluid handling. Its capabilities span material development, product concept design, precise prototyping, and a variety of manufacturing technologies under one roof, including clean room production. RAUMEDIC also provides regulatory support toward product registration. The firm notes "production sites worldwide" and "square meters of clean room production space," though specific figures are not given.

RAUMEDIC serves the medical technology and pharmaceutical sectors, with application areas including cardiosurgery, cell and gene therapy, drug delivery, enteral feeding, infusion, neuromonitoring, ophthalmology, orthopedics, pharma fluid handling, and traumatology. Customers range from biopharma companies needing single-use bioprocess equipment to device manufacturers requiring catheter systems for physiological monitoring.

The company emphasizes an integrated "Everything From One Source" approach, combining material expertise, design, manufacturing, and regulatory services. Sustainability is highlighted through on-site renewable energy generation — a biomass heating plant and roughly 2,500 solar panels at its German headquarters — and a green product development program using novel biopolymers to reduce carbon footprint.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','ISO 50001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Material development", "Product concept development", "Design and prototyping", "Manufacturing (variety of technologies)", "Regulatory support and product registration", "Clean room production", "Tubing and tubing systems for fluid handling", "Catheter manufacturing for neuromonitoring", "Single-use bioprocess equipment", "Sustainable/green product development"], "industries": ["Medical technology", "Pharmaceutical", "Biopharma", "Cardiosurgery", "Cell and gene therapy", "Drug delivery", "Enteral feeding", "Infusion therapy", "Neuromonitoring", "Ophthalmology", "Orthopedics", "Pharma fluid handling", "Traumatology"], "materials": ["Medical-grade polymers", "Biopolymers", "Drop-in biopolymers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Everything From One Source\" integration of material development, design, manufacturing, and regulatory support", "Polymer-based solutions for medical, pharmaceutical, and intensive care applications", "Clean room production across multiple global sites", "On-site renewable energy generation (biomass plant and 2,500 solar panels) at German headquarters", "Green product development using drop-in biopolymers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Mills River, North Carolina -> db", "German headquarters in Helmbrechts -> page /", "Polymer-based solutions for medical/pharma -> page /", "Capabilities: material development, product concepts, design/prototyping, manufacturing, regulatory support -> page /", "Application areas: cardiosurgery, cell/gene therapy, drug delivery, enteral feeding, infusion, neuromonitoring, ophthalmology, orthopedics, pharma fluid handling, traumatology -> page /", "Clean room production space, production sites worldwide -> page /", "Renewable energy: biomass heating plant and 2500 solar panels at German HQ -> page /", "ISO 14001 certification -> db", "ISO 50001 energy management -> page /", "Green product development using biopolymers -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We focus on polymer-based solutions for medical and pharmaceutical applications, as well as on products for intensive care.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='raumedic' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='RAYGUN operates from Des Moines, Iowa. According to company records, the business traces its origins to 1857, though the current retail brand appears to be a more recent incarnation.

The company runs an e-commerce storefront specializing in Des Moines and Iowa-themed apparel and accessories. Its catalog spans t-shirts, hoodies, hats, mugs, stickers, tote bags, pint glasses, and enamel pins. Designs reference local landmarks such as the Iowa Capitol and East Village, as well as collegiate partners including Drake University, Iowa State University, and the University of Iowa. The store also carries pride-themed items and humorous slogans like "Des Moines Hates Nazis" and "Des Moines Is Pretty Gay."

RAYGUN sells directly to consumers through its website and offers a pickup option for local customers.

