UPDATE companies SET description='Ratigan-Schottler Manufacturing has operated from the same workshop in Beatrice, Nebraska since its founding in 1940 by Louie Schottler. The company began as a woodworking shop serving local churches and has remained in the same location for over eight decades, drawing on the region’s tradition of fine craftsmanship.

The firm specializes in solid oak church furniture, producing custom pews, chancel furnishings, liturgical pieces, curved radius pews, and flexible seating. Its 65,000-square-foot facility houses state-of-the-art fabrication equipment where skilled craftsmen handle every step from lumber milling to final assembly. The company reports having served more than 2,500 churches and built over 500,000 linear feet of pews.

Customers are primarily Christian congregations across the United States, including projects in Hawaii. The company’s installation teams travel nationwide to deliver and anchor pews using a concealed anchor system. Past clients include churches in Oklahoma, Minnesota, Illinois, and Wisconsin, as noted in testimonials.

Ratigan-Schottler emphasizes three pillars—craftsmanship, service, and tradition—as its differentiators. It promotes an in-house design team that collaborates directly with clients, a seamless process from quote through follow-up, and a commitment to hand-selected northern hardwoods such as red oak, white oak, maple, mahogany, and cherry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom church pew design", "Solid oak fabrication", "Chancel furniture fabrication", "Curved radius pew fabrication", "Pew refinishing", "Pew restoration", "Flexible seating/chair fabrication", "Kneeler fabrication", "Installation services", "Concealed anchor installation", "Design consultation", "Project management from quote to follow-up"], "industries": ["Churches", "Religious institutions"], "materials": ["Red oak", "White oak", "Maple", "Mahogany", "Cherry", "Northern hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Turnaround times vary; immediate availability for certain jobs and short turnaround times for pew production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same workshop in Beatrice, Nebraska since 1940", "65,000 sq ft state-of-the-art fabrication facility", "Nationwide installation including Hawaii with concealed anchor system", "In-house design team managing projects from concept to installation", "Hand-selected northern hardwoods (red oak, white oak, maple, mahogany, cherry)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1940 by Louie Schottler -> /about", "Workshop in Beatrice, Nebraska since 1940 -> /", "65,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "2500+ churches served, 500,000+ feet of pews built -> /", "Nationwide installation including Hawaii -> /", "Materials: red oak, white oak, maple, mahogany, cherry -> /", "Concealed anchor system for pew installation -> /", "In-house design team -> /about", "Three core values: craftsmanship, service, tradition -> /", "Process: design, fabrication, installation, follow-up -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Fabrication: Lumber comes in from the mill and leaves our dock to your church ready for final assembly.", "founded_year": "1940", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ratigan-schottler-manufacturing/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ratigan-schottler-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Re-form was founded in 1986 in Beltsville, Maryland, after recognizing that businesses struggled to manage increasingly complex office furniture systems and often discarded usable assets. The company began by refurbishing furniture for large corporations and reselling high-quality used systems to smaller organizations across the Mid-Atlantic region, including Aberdeen, Baltimore, Columbia, and Washington, DC.

Today Re-form operates a 50,000-square-foot warehouse and production facility in Baltimore where nearly 50 skilled upholsterers, painters, woodworkers, warehouse technicians, installers, designers, and project managers handle warehousing, inventory management, furniture delivery and installation, office decommissioning, space planning, and furniture refurbishment. The facility supports remanufacturing of Herman Miller, Haworth, and Steelcase systems furniture, along with paint refinishing, seating reupholstery, and laminate fabrication. An online inventory portal gives clients remote access to stored assets and allows them to request delivery or installation.

The company serves enterprise-sized corporations, government agencies, and other organizations undergoing relocation, renovation, consolidation, or new-space openings throughout the Mid-Atlantic. It also taps a national installation network for out-of-state projects. Clients rely on Re-form for coordinated workplace transitions that encompass asset tracking, responsible reuse and recycling, and phased deployment.

Re-form positions itself as a single-source partner for workplace logistics, emphasizing practical, flexible solutions that reduce waste, control costs, and extend the useful life of existing furniture. Its combined services—warehousing, asset management, installation, decommissioning, and design—are intended to keep organizations organized and adaptable as workplace needs change.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Warehouse storage and inventory management", "Furniture delivery and installation", "Office decommissioning", "Space planning and workplace design", "Furniture refurbishment and repair", "Systems furniture remanufacturing", "Paint refinishing", "Seating reupholstery", "Laminate fabrication", "Asset management via online portal", "Project management", "Design services (AutoCAD)", "Office relocation and moving", "Phased deployment", "Receiving, photographing, and cataloging assets", "Reconfiguration of workstations", "Responsible reuse, recycling, and disposal"], "industries": ["Commercial office furniture", "Government agencies", "Enterprise corporations", "Mid-Atlantic region businesses"], "materials": ["Herman Miller systems furniture", "Haworth systems furniture", "Steelcase systems furniture", "Fabrics", "Laminates", "Paints"], "equipment": ["AutoCAD", "Specialty office furniture asset management software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["50,000 sq ft warehouse and production facility in Baltimore", "Nearly 50 skilled craftsmen on site daily", "Online inventory portal for remote asset management and request fulfillment", "National installation network for out-of-state deliveries", "Specializes in Herman Miller, Haworth, and Steelcase systems furniture"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1986 -> /about", "Headquarters in Beltsville, Maryland -> db", "50,000 sq ft warehouse and production facility in Baltimore -> /about", "Nearly 50 skilled workers at facility -> /about", "Services: warehousing, inventory management, delivery, installation, decommissioning, space planning, refurbishment -> /", "Specializes in Herman Miller, Haworth, Steelcase systems furniture -> /about", "Online inventory portal for remote asset management -> /", "National installation network for out-of-state deliveries -> /services", "Serves enterprise corporations and government agencies -> /about", "Mid-Atlantic region coverage (Aberdeen, Baltimore, Columbia, Washington DC) -> /about", "In-house project management and design with 50+ years combined experience -> /services", "Paint refinishing, seating reupholstery, laminate fabrication -> /about", "Responsible reuse, recycling, disposal emphasis -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Re-form helps organizations manage workplace transitions with warehousing, asset management, office decommissioning, furniture installation, and space planning services\u2014all coordinated through one experienced team.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "nearly 50", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='re-form-office-furniture-reseller-storage' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ReNu Solar & Roofing operates from Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, serving residential customers across central and eastern Pennsylvania and into Maryland. It has worked with insurance providers on hail and wind damage claims since 2012.

The firm provides turnkey solar, roofing, and battery storage installation for homeowners. Its process covers free in-home consultation, custom system design using CAD software, permitting, utility coordination, installation, and final inspection. ReNu handles all steps in-house, avoiding subcontractors, and partners with SolarEdge and Enphase for storage equipment. The company offers 25-year warranties on workmanship, full system performance, and energy production.

ReNu serves residential property owners in counties including Mifflin, Juniata, Snyder, Berks, and the areas around Philadelphia and Baltimore. Its customers are typically homeowners seeking to reduce electricity bills, sell excess power to utilities, and protect against rising energy rates. The company also assists with insurance claims for storm-damaged roofs.

ReNu differentiates itself through undivided responsibility—clients have a single point of contact for both roofing and solar work—and through its 25-year transferable warranties that include a watertight roof penetration guarantee. The firm emphasizes local, experienced staff and a streamlined, no-subcontractor model.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design and installation", "Roofing installation and repair", "Battery energy storage installation", "Insurance claim assistance for hail and wind damage", "Permitting and utility interconnection coordination", "Custom solar layout design using CAD", "Free in-home energy consultation"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Residential roofing", "Residential energy storage", "Insurance restoration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single point of contact for roofing and solar (no subcontractors)", "25-year warranties on workmanship, system, and production", "Installation partnerships with SolarEdge and Enphase", "Full permitting and utility coordination handled in-house", "Free in-home consultation and custom CAD design"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania -> db", "Works with insurance providers since 2012 -> db", "Roots in roofing, expanded to solar -> /services", "Services areas across Pennsylvania and Maryland -> /", "Offers solar, roofing, storage installation -> /services", "No subcontractors, undivided responsibility -> /services", "25-year warranties on workmanship, full system, production -> /services", "Partners with SolarEdge and Enphase for storage -> /services", "Handles permits, engineering, installation, inspections -> /services", "Free in-home consultation and custom CAD design -> /services", "Residential customers in specific PA counties and MD -> /", "Assists with insurance claims for hail/wind damage -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a solar and roofing company changing homes in the areas we service. We install high quality and sustainable solar panels that will reduce your electric bill and increase your eco-friendly contributions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='renu-solar-roofing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Reclaiming Iowa operates from West Des Moines, Iowa, where it was founded in 2008 by Kevin Dubay. Dubay holds a Bachelor of Fine Arts from the Kansas City Art Institute and a Master''s in Furniture Design and Manufacturing from the University of Arizona, and he launched the studio to combine artistic vision with hands-on craftsmanship.

The company builds custom commercial and residential heirloom furniture and architectural woodwork using locally sourced reclaimed timbers and live‑edge hardwood slabs. Every piece is made to order — about 90 percent of projects are fully custom — and the workshop handles everything from consultation and design through handcrafting, kiln‑drying slabs to 6 percent moisture content, and finishing with a durable hard wax oil. Restoration services are not offered.

Clients span residential homeowners and a range of commercial sectors: restaurants and bars (dining tables, bar tops, back bars, feature walls), retail (countertops, shelving, product displays), and office or flex spaces (conference tables, desks, reception pieces). The studio has completed projects for businesses across Iowa, delivering and installing each piece statewide at no extra charge.

Dubay started Reclaiming Iowa to provide furniture that fits a client''s exact space and style while preserving the history of salvaged wood. When possible, pieces are labeled with the original building name, location, and construction date, turning each item into a conversation piece and an environmentally sustainable choice.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and build", "Commercial woodwork", "Residential furniture", "Live edge tables", "Farmhouse tables", "Extendable tables", "Matching benches", "Bar tops", "Back bars", "Feature walls", "Countertops", "Shelving", "Product displays", "Conference tables", "Desks", "Built-ins", "Kiln drying", "Hard wax oil finishing", "Handcrafted joinery (biscuit, pocket screw)", "Consultation and design", "Free statewide delivery and installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Restaurants and Bars", "Retail", "Office and Flex Spaces", "Hospitality"], "materials": ["Reclaimed timbers", "Hardwood slabs", "Walnut", "Live-edge hardwood", "Native Iowa wood species"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free statewide delivery included on every custom order", "Hard wax oil finish that enhances grain and provides long\u2011lasting protection", "Reclaimed timbers sourced from buildings and barns over 100 years old, with provenance labeling", "Kiln\u2011dried hardwood slabs to 6% moisture content for stability", "90% of projects are fully custom, built to client specifications"], "facts_used": ["Location: West Des Moines, Iowa -> db", "Founded: 2008 -> db", "Founder: Kevin Dubay -> /about", "Founder education: BFA Kansas City Art Institute, Master''s University of Arizona -> /about", "Specializes in custom heirloom furniture from reclaimed timbers and hardwoods -> /", "90% custom projects -> /", "No restoration services -> /", "Kiln-dry to 6% moisture -> /about", "Hard wax oil finish -> /about", "Provenance labeling of reclaimed wood -> /about", "Free statewide delivery -> /", "Commercial sectors: restaurants, bars, retail, office -> /services", "Residential products: dining tables, coffee tables, desks, built-ins -> /services", "Process: consultation, design, build, deliver -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Reclaiming Iowa specializes in custom commercial and residential heirloom furniture and decor made from locally sourced reclaimed timbers and hardwoods.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='reclaiming-iowa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Red Fox Innovations was founded in 2015 in Blaine, Minnesota, as a domestic response to the offshoring of cut-and-sew work. The company began with a focus on providing reliable, cost-competitive manufacturing without sacrificing quality, and has since grown into a full-service contract manufacturer.

Today the firm operates an FDA-registered, ISO 13485-certified facility where over 160 employees produce more than one million units annually across 1,000-plus unique product designs. All work is performed on-site using automated fabric cutters, programmable sewing machines, large-format RF welding equipment, and laser cutting systems. Services span industrial sewing, die and laser cutting, RF/ultrasonic/hot-air welding, material sourcing, and full product design and development from prototype to volume production.

The customer base ranges from large public corporations to start-ups, with core markets in medical devices, outdoor and specialty retail, and military/government contracts requiring Berry Amendment compliance. The company also supports direct-to-consumer brands seeking U.S.-made soft goods.

Red Fox merged with major client Caerus Corp in 2022 to combine resources under brands such as Animal Ortho Care and OrthoCor Medical. The founding philosophy — “we succeed when our customers succeed” — remains central, reinforced by proprietary factory-management software that tracks real-time productivity and quality metrics at every workstation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial sewing (straight stitch, zigzag, overlock, programmable large-format)", "Automated fabric cutting (laser, die, knife)", "Laser cutting (metals, plastics, specialty textiles)", "Radio Frequency (RF) welding (large format, high power)", "Ultrasonic welding", "Hot air welding", "Material sourcing and supply planning", "Product design and development (concept to prototype to production)", "Contract textile/fabric cutting services", "Cut and sew contract manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Outdoor / retail", "Military / government", "Direct-to-consumer retail"], "materials": ["Textiles", "Buckles", "Webbing", "Zippers", "Hook and loop fasteners", "Custom brand embellishments", "Snaps", "High-tech closures", "Specialty textiles", "Metals (for laser cutting)", "Plastics (for laser cutting)"], "equipment": ["Automated fabric cutters", "Programmable sewing machines", "Large-format RF welding machines", "Laser cutting equipment", "Ultrasonic welding equipment", "Hot air welding equipment"], "volume": "1,000,000+ units annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA-registered and ISO 13485-certified facility with 100% on-site manufacturing", "Proprietary real-time factory management software tracking efficiency and hourly quality", "Berry Amendment compliance for U.S. government contracts", "Over 160 direct employees and automated cutting/sewing equipment for high-volume scale", "Merged with Caerus Corp (2022) to leverage combined resources and brands"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2015 in Blaine, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Over 160 direct employees -> /", "1,000,000+ annual production units -> /", "100% manufactured on site -> /", "FDA Registered and ISO 13485 Certified facility -> /", "Industries: medical devices, outdoor/retail, military/government -> /", "Berry Compliance for US Government business -> /", "Merged with Caerus Corp in 2022 -> /about-us", "Proprietary factory management software with real-time metrics -> /", "Capabilities: industrial sewing, automated cutting, RF welding, ultrasonic welding, hot air welding, laser cutting, die cutting, material sourcing, product development -> /services", "Equipment: automated fabric cutters, programmable sewing machines, large format RF welding machines, laser cutting equipment -> /, /services", "Materials: textiles, buckles, webbing, zippers, hook/loop, snaps, high-tech closures -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cut and Sew Contract Manufacturer", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "160+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='red-fox-innovations' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Red Oak Fabrication operates from Red Oak, Iowa, where it was established in 1913 as the Pike Machine Shop. Renamed Red Oak Machine Co. in 1923, the business was purchased by Ted Fort in stages between 1944 and 1946 and has remained in the Fort family for four generations. Today the company runs four facilities in southwest Iowa, with Jeff Fort and his three sons — Jacob, Jordan, and Justin — serving as owners and managers.

The shop provides a full range of metal fabrication services: plasma cutting on two Alltra tables (up to 3-inch capacity), fiber laser cutting with three Bystronic and Cutlite systems (including the first Cutlite Penta 20 kW in the U.S. with fully automated load/unload), tube laser cutting, CNC milling and turning across 11 machining centers, press brake forming up to 350 tons, robotic and manual welding (11 AWS D1.1‑certified welders), steel blasting, and powder coating. The powder coating line uses the only GFS booths in Iowa that combine blasting with a three‑stage wash, and is certified to AAMA 2603, 2604, and 2605.

Red Oak Fabrication serves industrial and commercial customers requiring precision metal parts, welded assemblies, and finished coatings.

The company emphasizes its multi‑generational family ownership, direct owner involvement in daily operations, and unique powder‑coating capabilities — particularly the combined blast‑and‑wash booth and 60‑color in‑house palette with custom matching in 10 business days. Turnaround for coating is typically 7–10 days, with 24‑hour expedited service available.', certifications=ARRAY['AAMA 2603','AAMA 2604','AAMA 2605','AWS D1.1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plasma cutting", "Fiber laser cutting", "Tube laser cutting", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "CNC machining", "Robotic welding", "Manual welding", "Powder coating", "Steel blasting", "High\u2011temperature burn off", "Press brake forming", "Assembly", "Automated bandsawing", "CNC lathe with subspindle & Y\u2011axis", "Horizontal milling", "Vertical milling", "Automated blast cleaning", "Manual blast booth", "Powder coat batch processing", "Custom color matching", "AAMA 2603/2604/2605 certified powder coating"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "UHMW"], "equipment": ["Alltra plasma table w/ Hypertherm XPR 300 (12''x24'')", "Alltra plasma table w/ Hypertherm HPR 400 (12''x24'')", "Bystronic BySmart Fiber 3015 6 kW", "Bystronic BySmart Fiber 3015 10 kW", "Cutlite Penta Fiber Fast 4020 20 kW", "Bystronic M3 FL300 Tube Laser", "Bystronic Xpert320 350 ton 14 ft press brake", "Bystronic Xpert80 80 ton 5 ft press brake (2)", "Bystronic Xpert320 350 ton 13 ft 6 in press brake", "80 ton horizontal press", "Genesis Systems robotic weld stations (2)", "Universal Robots welding cobot (4''x8'' working area)", "Fronius pulse welding stations (10)", "VF 10 Haas machining center", "Flex Arm tapping arms (2)", "Automated bandsaws", "Clemco/GFS manual blast booths 14''x24'' (2)", "Clemco manual blast cabinet 4''x6'' with 48\" turntable", "Viking 84T automated blast cabinet", "Gibson 96XT automated blast cabinet", "GFS batch powder coat lines with overhead rail (3)", "Wash booth 4\u2011stag